@title Borrowing at Millbrook Public Library
@subtitle Frequently asked questions, effective 2026-11-01
@author Hye-jin Park, Circulation Manager

! From 2026-11-01, the library no longer charges late fines.

## Who can join the library?

Membership is free. Anyone who lives, works or studies in Millbrook County can join.

Children under 18 need a parent or guardian to sign up.

## How many items can I borrow?

You can borrow up to 30 items at once. Within that limit:

- At most 5 can be DVDs.
- At most 2 can be Wi-Fi hotspots.

## How long can I keep things?

table = item,loan period; Books and audiobooks,21 days; DVDs,7 days; Wi-Fi hotspots,14 days

## What if I return something late?

There are no late fines from 2026-11-01. Here is what to know:

- An item that is 30 days overdue is treated as lost. We charge its replacement cost, capped at $25 an item.
- Borrowing is paused while your account owes $10 or more.

## How do I renew?

You can renew online, in the app or at the desk. You can renew up to 3 times, unless another reader is waiting.

## How do I reserve an item?

Reservations are free. You can have up to 15 at once.

We email you when your item is ready. It waits at the desk for 7 days.

---

Questions? Email help@millbrooklibrary.example or visit the desk on weekdays from 09:00 to 18:00.
